30
00:01:32,650 --> 00:01:38,310
Okay, well, a Christmas tree is usually a green tree that we cut down and we put in the house.

31
00:01:38,310 --> 00:01:41,150
Okay, so it's not a real tree with the roots in the ground.

32
00:01:41,150 --> 00:01:43,530
But sometimes it comes from a real tree outside.

33
00:01:44,590 --> 00:01:48,550
And the tree is very small on the top and it goes out like a triangle.

34
00:01:49,390 --> 00:01:50,410
Okay, so it's a special shape.

35
00:01:51,010 --> 00:01:56,870
And we generally make it look very pretty with lights and ornaments and decorations.

36
00:01:57,770 --> 00:02:05,190
And on Christmas, on the 25th or the 24th, it depends where you come from, we put lots of presents underneath the Christmas tree.

37
00:02:05,490 --> 00:02:06,930
Wow, it sounds amazing.

38
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:09,480
Well, yeah, and it looks very nice.

39
00:02:09,480 --> 00:02:10,370
It does look really beautiful.

40
00:02:10,480 --> 00:02:12,590
And it's just a really special part of Christmas.

41
00:02:13,180 --> 00:02:16,890
And well, as you mentioned, sometimes the tree is just a fake plastic tree.

42
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:21,950
But many times it's a real tree and the type of tree that you use is a pine tree.

43
00:02:22,440 --> 00:02:22,590
Exactly.

44
00:02:23,440 --> 00:02:26,520
And so pine tree is a kind of tree that doesn't have leaves.

45
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:28,160
It has needles.

46
00:02:28,160 --> 00:02:33,610
That means that they're long, very thin green pieces that are all over the tree.

47
00:02:34,700 --> 00:02:44,800
And you can see these trees in most northern places like Scandinavia or in America, maybe Illinois and Minnesota and Michigan and Vermont.

48
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:50,470
And they're very, as you say, very unique trees, but they also have a very special smell, the smell of pine.

49
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:51,170
They do.

50
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:52,880
It's very nice.

51
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:59,150
It's such a nice smell that a lot of the things that we use in America to clean our houses have a pine smell because it makes the house smell nice.

52
00:02:59,840 --> 00:03:00,030
Very good.

53
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:01,650
So a pine tree.

54
00:03:02,200 --> 00:03:09,390
The dad brought a pine tree or a Christmas tree home and well, the wife was a little bit worried if it will fit.

55
00:03:09,990 --> 00:03:11,570
Okay, will it fit?

56
00:03:11,890 --> 00:03:15,210
This is a very important question because a lot of pine trees are very, very tall.

57
00:03:16,070 --> 00:03:22,290
So if a pine tree is three meters tall or four meters tall, will it fit is the question we ask.

58
00:03:22,510 --> 00:03:27,720
Is it too big or is it going to be stuck on the ceiling in the house?

59
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:30,880
